You’re right. It is not a double reimbursement. The situation is that you were reimbursed once based on what you believed was a personal-card payment, but the actual hotel charge ultimately went to your corporate card and is currently sitting unsubmitted in Concur.

So the question for Finance is how to properly reconcile the prior reimbursement with the corporate-card transaction. I’d revise the email this way:

Hi Finance Team,

I’m looking for guidance on how to correct a hotel expense.

In August, I booked a hotel for the Posit Conference in Houston (Sept. 14–16). Since my corporate card had expired, I used my personal card for the reservation. The hotel sent me a receipt, so I believed my personal card had been charged. I submitted the expense in Concur as a personal expense, and it was approved and reimbursed in my August 31 paycheck.

When I checked in on Sept. 14, I added my new corporate card to the hotel profile. At checkout, the hotel charged the full amount to my corporate card. It appears the earlier transaction on my personal card was only a hold/deposit, not an actual charge.

The corporate card transaction is now sitting in Concur and has not been submitted. What is the best way to correct this? Can I pay the corporate card charge personally, or should I submit it through Concur and have the amount previously reimbursed on Aug. 31 deducted from my next paycheck?

Thank you for your guidance.

Best,
Derek

This version makes it clear that there has only been one reimbursement so far and that you’re asking Finance how to reconcile the outstanding corporate-card charge.